Reviews shows the harsh review rounds of a checkout's next commit

Tama's review-commit lets a commit through only once a reviewer that is
not its author recorded a round over the exact staged tree and message
that found nothing. The Reviews screen gains a Harsh review rounds panel:
given a checkout path it reads the native reviews/harsh request and
lists each round with its reviewer, staged tree and findings, and each
finding recorded as a defect. An entry or reviewer of a kind the panel
does not know fails to decode with that kind named, and a failed read is
shown and reported under tama.reviews.harsh.

